# kex: check-only
# `is?` takes a type or a trait, named as written: a value is no type to test
# against (KEXET-0515). A trait that holds by a type's shape (Showable: every
# value shows) has no list of types to test, so it is refused too (KEXET-0516).

main do
  let kind = "String"
  let v = 3
  IO.printLine(v.is?(kind))
  IO.printLine(v.is?(Showable))
  IO.printLine(v.is?(String))
end
